  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="CC Modifier" id="1f11-635b-21fb-f93c" hidden="false">
      <description>If a model bears a weapon with this keyword, change the Close Combat characteristic of that model by x, with x being the value at the end of this rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Parry" id="a3ea-796c-328a-c8ff" hidden="false">
      <description>When an enemy model declares damage made with a melee weapon against a model with at least one Parry weapon, roll one D6 for every point of damage to be inflicted. On a 5+, that damage is instead allocated to the enemy model. When allocating damage, any models in the unit without a Parry weapon must be selected first.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Quick Turn" id="c1d1-d3e7-459b-b523" hidden="false">
      <description>If every model in a unit has this rule, they are able to perform a Quick Turn during their movement phase. To perform a Quick Turn, a model must perform a movement a number of inches below it&apos;s total Movement characteristic. It may then pivot in any direction and perform a movement equal to or less than the remainder of their total Movement characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Frontline Assault Force" id="12a9-e350-f80c-ac51" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit in your army performs an Advance move, if the result of that Advance roll is less than 4, that unit may choose to either shoot or charge this turn, it cannot do both unless a unit or weapon ability/keyword states otherwise. Additionally, if a unit Remained Stationary, they receive an improvement of 1 to their Save Roll characteristic (to a maximum of 3+).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
